(ARG-12 — the Checking if Arguments Were Provided example
 (LANGUAGE.md:4758-4760), verbatim: `arguments's empty` used directly as
 an If condition, with no comparison. Run with no arguments, so the
 branch is taken. The Otherwise arm is this probe's own addition, so
 that the recorded block proves which arm ran rather than proving only
 that nothing was printed.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-12.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   No arguments provided.
)
If arguments's empty then,
    Print "No arguments provided.".
Otherwise,
    Print "Arguments were provided.".
